title: "MeanFieldHomogenization.jl: Mean-field homogenization of heterogeneous materials"
abstract: "Julia framework for mean-field homogenization of heterogeneous materials. Provides Hill polarization tensors for ellipsoidal inclusions (2D/3D, isotropic and anisotropic matrices), crack-opening-displacement tensors, stress and displacement intensity factors for flat cracks, and second-order Hill tensors for transport problems, under a common abstraction hierarchy and dispatch mechanism. A microstructure can also be used directly as a constitutive law at each Gauss point of a finite-element computation, including the poroelastic coefficients and the permeability of a fractured rock whose fractures open and close under load. Linear viscoelasticity is available both as an ageing time-domain Volterra pipeline and through the Laplace-Carson correspondence principle, with autodiff-capable numerical inverse Laplace transforms, a catalogue of rheological models and the exact generalized-Kelvin/generalized-Maxwell conversion. ForwardDiff-compatible across every analytical and DECUHR path."
